
Description:

iSchedule is now used only between the backends of a Cyrus Murder, and a
backend accepts it only from servers listed in proxyservers.  Standalone
servers and frontends no longer offer an iSchedule receiver, and the
never-built DKIM support and /domainkeys resource are gone.


Documentation:

docsrc/download/installation/http/caldav.rst


Config changes:

The "ischedule" and "domainkey" values are no longer valid in the
httpmodules option.

The ischedule_dkim_domain, ischedule_dkim_key_file,
ischedule_dkim_required and ischedule_dkim_selector options have been
deprecated.


Upgrade instructions:

Remove "ischedule" and "domainkey" from httpmodules, if present.  httpd
will refuse to start with either of them.


GitHub issue:

None.
